\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The two events of Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:event}}, the unattributed crossings whose stellar statistic exceeds all 512{} control positions of their own window. Repeat epochs measured are the blocks at which the predicted stellar-frame cell was read; the indented rows give how many of those the released catalogue carries and how many blocks it lists as covering the frequency at all, which differ because the archival extension is deposited separately. The two measured values are different readings of one cell --- at the matched drift, which is one cell and one trial and may therefore be negative, and maximised over every drift trial, which is larger by construction. The exclusion is formed from the first.}}{12}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
